  "rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last 1–2 weeks show a sustained rise, the model level is systematically too low versus realized prices across almost the entire 30D horizon.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: errors grow with lead time (small in days 1–3, large by days 7–30). Apply an increasing upward adjustment with horizon during bullish regimes.",
    "Lag in trend acceleration: the model captures direction but reacts too slowly to rapid step-ups; realized prices re-rate higher earlier than forecast (especially around days 5–15).",
    "Over-mean-reversion / capped upside: forecasts repeatedly drift back toward ~68–71 even while outcomes continue trending to ~75–83, indicating an implicit ceiling. Remove/relax the cap and allow higher terminal levels when momentum is positive.",
    "Post-spike behavior: after sharp realized run-ups, the model tends to fade/flatten too quickly (predicts consolidation) while outcomes keep grinding higher; reduce fade strength after upside breaks."
  ]
}
